<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Material 3 fade, screen that is ARRIVING (push: the new screen; pop: the one
  revealed underneath).

  Same file name as a react-native-screens resource: an app resource replaces
  the library's one when Gradle merges resources, so react-native-screens
  (4.28.0, pinned in package.json) runs this without being patched. The stock
  file is a plain 150ms crossfade that runs in parallel with the outgoing one.

  M3 values, from MaterialFadeThrough / motionDurationLong1:
    duration  300ms, alpha and scale on the same clock
    easing    emphasized, cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1) -> ../interpolator/pixi_emphasized.xml
    scale     comes in from 0.92 of full size (ScaleProvider's incomingStartScale)

  ## Why there is no startOffset

  The literal fade-through split (MDC's FADE_THROUGH_THRESHOLD, 0.35) held this
  screen at alpha 0 for the first 105ms, so it only appeared once the outgoing
  one was already gone. Measured on the emphasized curve the outgoing screen is
  ~90% transparent by 56ms, which left a ~50ms frame of *nothing* between the
  two, and a tap that visibly did nothing for the first tenth of a second — it
  read as "the page opens slowly", on exactly the two screens that switch most
  (Home, Browse). Starting together turns the gap into a crossfade: content is
  ~60% in after 60ms and 90% in by 150ms, on the same 300ms Material budget.

  The scale is about the centre and `colors.background` is the same #101214 as
  `colors.surface`, so the ring it briefly opens around the content is invisible.

  Assigned to `animation: 'fade'` by src/navigation/RootNavigator.tsx.

  Re-check this file when react-native-screens is bumped: a qualifier-specific
  variant (anim-v33/…) or a rename would stop this override winning, silently.
-->
<set xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shareInterpolator="false">
    <alpha
        android:fromAlpha="0"
        android:toAlpha="1"
        android:startOffset="0"
        android:duration="300"
        android:interpolator="@interpolator/pixi_emphasized" />
    <scale
        android:fromXScale="0.92"
        android:toXScale="1"
        android:fromYScale="0.92"
        android:toYScale="1"
        android:pivotX="50%"
        android:pivotY="50%"
        android:startOffset="0"
        android:duration="300"
        android:interpolator="@interpolator/pixi_emphasized" />
</set>
